# Bucket 1 Q4 — v1.1.0 memorySearch default-injection check

> Date: 2026-05-13
> Branch: `ralph/memorysearch-decision`
> Question (from `docs/1.1.0-upgrade-followups.md` Bucket 1 Q4):
>   Does `hiclaw-manager:v1.1.0` still inject `agents.defaults.memorySearch`
>   defaults into `openclaw.json`? If not, the `pop('memorySearch')` line in
>   `manager-init-internal.sh` can simply be deleted.

## Verdict

Two defense layers exist today:

| Layer | Location | Behaviour in v1.1.0 |
|---|---|---|
| A | `deploy/docker/docker-compose.yaml` — `HICLAW_EMBEDDING_MODEL=` (empty) | **LOAD-BEARING.** Keep. |
| B | `deploy/hiclaw/manager-init-internal.sh` — Python `pop('memorySearch')` | **Dead code in v1.1.0.** Removed in this branch. |

Layer A is load-bearing because `/opt/hiclaw/scripts/lib/hiclaw-env.sh` uses
single-dash `${VAR-default}` semantics that fall back to a broken default when
the env var is unset:

```sh
HICLAW_EMBEDDING_MODEL="${HICLAW_EMBEDDING_MODEL-text-embedding-v4}"
```

`text-embedding-v4` against the AI gateway (DashScope coding endpoint) has no
`/v1/embeddings` route, so injection would abort the Manager agent run before
any chat call.

Layer B is dead because `start-manager-agent.sh` only injects memorySearch when
`$emb_model != ""`:

```sh
| if $emb_model != "" then .agents.defaults.memorySearch //= {...} else . end
```

With Layer A set to empty string, the upstream `openclaw.json` never contains
memorySearch in the first place, so the Python `pop()` is a no-op.

## Empirical evidence (collected from the running v1.1.0 stack)

```
$ docker exec honeybadge-hiclaw-manager env | grep -E "EMBEDDING|HICLAW_AI_GATEWAY"
HICLAW_AI_GATEWAY_URL=http://aigw-local.hiclaw.io:8080
HICLAW_AI_GATEWAY_DOMAIN=aigw-local.hiclaw.io
HICLAW_EMBEDDING_MODEL=

$ for f in /root/manager-workspace/openclaw.json \
           /root/hiclaw-fs/manager/openclaw.json \
           /root/hiclaw-fs/agents/manager/openclaw.json; do
    echo "$f: $(grep -c memorySearch $f)"
  done
/root/manager-workspace/openclaw.json: 0
/root/hiclaw-fs/manager/openclaw.json: 0
/root/hiclaw-fs/agents/manager/openclaw.json: 0

$ docker logs honeybadge-hiclaw-manager 2>&1 | grep "Removed agents.defaults.memorySearch"
(no output — pop() never fired)

$ grep -c memorySearch /opt/hiclaw/configs/manager-openclaw.json.tmpl
0
```

## Worker side

Worker `openclaw.json` is regenerated by
`/opt/hiclaw/agent/skills/worker-management/scripts/generate-worker-config.sh`
which uses the same `if $emb_model != ""` guard. Confirmed on a live worker:

```
$ docker exec honeybadge-graph-worker grep -c memorySearch \
    /root/hiclaw-fs/agents/graph-worker/openclaw.json \
    /root/.openclaw/openclaw.json
/root/hiclaw-fs/agents/graph-worker/openclaw.json:0
/root/.openclaw/openclaw.json:0
```

## Action taken on this branch

1. Removed the dead `pop('memorySearch')` block from
   `deploy/hiclaw/manager-init-internal.sh` (was lines 652–660).
2. Sharpened the comment on `HICLAW_EMBEDDING_MODEL=` in
   `deploy/docker/docker-compose.yaml` to explicitly call out the
   `${VAR-default}` semantics, so future readers don't drop the empty-string
   value thinking it's a no-op.
3. Closed Bucket 1 Q4 in `docs/1.1.0-upgrade-followups.md`. Q1–Q3 still need
   product-level decisions and remain open.

## What remains open

- **Q1** SOUL.md ban granularity (full ban vs operational-only).
- **Q2** Higress `/v1/embeddings` upstream choice (DashScope `text-embedding-v4`
  vs MiniMax `embo-01` vs Ollama `bge-m3`).
- **Q3** Memory-file write strategy + audit-log integration.

These can move forward independently — they are product decisions, not blocked
on any v1.1.0 mechanics finding.
